# =============================================================================
# HueyOS kernel config fragment: v100-workstation
# =============================================================================
#
# This file is NOT a complete .config. It is a small, additive fragment that
# is merged with the Debian base config for the selected kernel source and
# resolved with `make olddefconfig` (see src/huey/kernel_build/config_builder.py,
# Step 11).
#
# The fragment only records the *intentional* deltas for this workstation:
#
#   Host:      Intel i9-12900K, ASUS TUF Z790-PLUS WIFI, Debian Forky
#   Display:   AMD RX 570, amdgpu, GNOME/Wayland  (must remain the display GPU)
#   Compute:   Tesla V100-PCIE-32GB, Volta sm_70, NVIDIA proprietary R580
#
# Every other subsystem -- storage controllers, PCIe, IOMMU, NVMe, AHCI, USB,
# ext4/Btrfs, networking, CPU frequency, and thermal -- is inherited unchanged
# from the Debian base config. Do not add those here; they are the base config's
# responsibility and the config builder's diff report will surface any changes.
#
# See kernel/huey-linux/README.md §13 for the interaction with
# src/huey/core/lab.config.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DRM / GPU
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Disable Nouveau for this profile.
#
# The Tesla V100 must be claimed by the proprietary NVIDIA module, not by
# Nouveau. If Nouveau is enabled (`=y` or `=m` with early KMS), it can bind
# the V100 at boot and the proprietary nvidia module will fail to initialize
# the GPU. Ubuntu's linux-nvidia kernel disables Nouveau with the explicit
# annotation "Disable nouveau for NVIDIA kernels" (CONFIG_DRM_NOUVEAU=n on
# amd64 and arm64) [5].
#
# `src/huey/core/lab.config` sets CONFIG_DRM_NOUVEAU=y. That fragment must
# NOT be applied unmodified to this profile. This line deliberately overrides
# it during merge_config.sh.
#
# CONFIG_DRM_NOUVEAU is not set

# Keep AMDGPU as a module.
#
# The RX 570 remains the display GPU. Building amdgpu as a module (=m) lets it
# load after the root filesystem is available and avoids forcing firmware into
# the kernel image or into the initramfs for the display path. Arch and Gentoo
# both recommend the module form for this reason [1][6].
#
# Do NOT set CONFIG_DRM_AMDGPU=y here. If a future requirement forces it into
# the kernel image, that change must be reviewed separately together with the
# firmware packaging plan for the RX 570.
CONFIG_DRM_AMDGPU=m

# Southern Islands / Sea Islands support is not required for Polaris (RX 570),
# but leaving them at Debian defaults is safer than forcing them off, because
# the V100 has no display output and this card is the only GPU that drives a
# monitor. Keep the Debian base-config values for these two symbols.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Loadable modules and external module support
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# External modules require CONFIG_MODULES.
CONFIG_MODULES=y

# CONFIG_MODVERSIONS must be enabled for the proprietary NVIDIA build.
#
# The NVIDIA kernel-module build needs Module.symvers CRCs to link against the
# exact kernel. A kernel built with CONFIG_MODVERSIONS=y produces those CRCs;
# a build that only runs `modules_prepare` does NOT produce Module.symvers even
# when CONFIG_MODVERSIONS is set, so the kernel must be fully built before the
# NVIDIA module can be compiled [4].
CONFIG_MODVERSIONS=y

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Guard: do not add these here
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The following are inherited from the Debian base config and must remain
# untouched by this fragment. If a change is ever needed, it belongs in a
# separate, reviewed fragment with its own rationale:
#
#   CONFIG_EXT4_FS, CONFIG_BTRFS_FS          (root filesystem)
#   CONFIG_NVME_CORE, CONFIG_BLK_DEV_NVME    (NVMe storage)
#   CONFIG_SATA_AHCI                         (SATA storage)
#   CONFIG_PCI, CONFIG_PCI_MSI               (PCIe)
#   CONFIG_INTEL_IOMMU, CONFIG_IOMMU_SUPPORT (IOMMU / VFIO if needed later)
#   CONFIG_USB_SUPPORT, CONFIG_USB_XHCI_HCD  (USB)
#   CONFIG_E1000E, CONFIG_IGC                (Intel Ethernet on Z790)
#   CONFIG_DRM_I915                          (Intel iGPU fallback; leave as base)
